        "content": "Design phase research completed. Explored full session infrastructure:\n\n**What exists:**\n- 37 session logs, 372K+ events in .kspec/sessions/\n- Each session: session.yaml (metadata), events.jsonl (JSONL event log), context-iter-N.json (snapshots)\n- Event types: session.start/update/end, prompt.sent, tool.call/result, note\n- Existing spec: @session-events covers storage layer (7 ACs, all implemented)\n- No CLI commands to query/analyze session data\n\n**Proposed specs (3):**\n1. session-log-list — List sessions with summary stats (status, duration, event count, task completions)\n2. session-log-show — Show detailed session view (events timeline, task transitions, iteration summaries)  \n3. session-log-stats — Aggregate analytics across sessions (throughput, duration trends, success rates)\n\n**Traits:** @json-output, @semantic-exit-codes on all three\n\n**Open design questions (awaiting user input):**\n1. Scope: all 3 specs or start with list+show?\n2. Naming: `kspec session log list` (sub-sub) vs `kspec session list` (direct subcommand)?\n3. Stats depth: simple counts vs deeper analysis (failure rates, tool patterns, iteration efficiency)?\n\n**Workflow state:** @spec-plan-design started (run 01KGTMBK), paused at design review step pending user decisions on scope/naming/depth.",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KGTMR4PKWKADDGSTFK312FGD",
        "created_at": "2026-02-06T23:31:43.956Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Plan document written and dry-run validated successfully. Ready to import.\n\n**Plan document:** /tmp scratchpad (session-log-analysis.md) — will need to be recreated if session expires.\n\n**Dry-run output confirmed:**\n- 4 specs: @session-log-list, @session-log-show, @session-log-stats, @session-log-search\n- 4 derived tasks: implement-session-log-{list,show,stats,search}\n- All under @session-events parent in @cli module\n- Traits: @json-output + @semantic-exit-codes on all, @filterable-list on list\n\n**Next step:** Run `kspec plan import <path> --module @cli` to create specs and tasks, then complete this design task.\n\n**Design decisions made:**\n- Namespace: kspec session log <subcommand> (avoids collision with session start/checkpoint)\n- All 4 commands (list/show/stats/search)\n- Deep stats (tool usage, time grouping) but bounded by structured data\n- Search supports filtering by event type, agent, date range\n- Shared infra: lazy JSONL reader, date filter utility, session ID prefix resolver",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KGTMYKBPBES529VVSJAVN5F8",
        "created_at": "2026-02-06T23:35:15.574Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Codex review completed and all feedback addressed:\n- MUST-FIX: Fixed trait refs to use full slugs (trait-json-output, trait-semantic-exit-codes, trait-filterable-list)\n- SHOULD-FIX: Added per-spec implementation_notes to show/stats/search specs\n- SHOULD-FIX: Made search excerpt concrete (200 chars) and added default limit (50 matches)\n- SHOULD-FIX: Split compound AC in stats (totals vs averages now separate ACs)\n- Scoped tool-usage output to top 10\n\nDry-run passes cleanly: 4 specs, 4 derived tasks under @session-events in @cli module.\n\nPlan document at scratchpad path (session-specific). Awaiting user confirmation to run import.\n\nNext: kspec plan import <path> --module @cli",
        "supersedes": null
      }
    ],
